I'm gonna let this pasta hang out.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:28.000
Can kind of like dry out
a little and then move on.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.770
So now I'm gonna cook my shrimp.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.640
I strain this shrimp stock.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.020
I'm gonna poach the shrimp in the stock.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.300
Since the stock is heated up.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.810
Just gonna add the shrimp right in.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:38.630
Poaching is a really
nice way to cook shrimp.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.810
I mean look how fast it goes.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:41.460
It's already starting to turn pink.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.866
Just gonna let that
cook for another minute.

00:09:42.866 --> 00:09:44.730
It's looking really good.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:45.563
Shrimp is done.

00:09:45.563 --> 00:09:47.386
I'm gonna keep the broth
just off to the side.

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:49.818
My shrimp are ready to go
and now all I have to do

00:09:49.818 --> 00:09:50.723
is boil the pasta.

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:52.836
Just gonna add a little
bit more salt to it

00:09:52.836 --> 00:09:54.210
and cook the pasta.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:56.270
When you're making
homemade pasta the joy is

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.870
that it cooks really quickly.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.140
Just wanna kind of gently twirl it

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.620
just so it doesn't stick together.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.960
Basically when it starts to
float and come to the top

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:04.793
you're done.

00:10:04.793 --> 00:10:07.150
Ooh, the texture is a little weird.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.154
I don't love it.

00:10:08.154 --> 00:10:09.180
Doesn't really tastes like pasta.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.420
I don't know guys.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.283
It's kind of sticking together.

00:10:11.283 --> 00:10:14.476
Let me add a few shrimp,
maybe that'll salvage.

00:10:14.476 --> 00:10:16.495
I think for the ingredients I have,

00:10:16.495 --> 00:10:18.633
I've done the best I can.

00:10:18.633 --> 00:10:20.650
I just wanna add a little of the broth.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:21.730
This is gonna help, I think.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.395
Maybe a little olive oil, little salt.

00:10:23.395 --> 00:10:24.900
And then I thought I would just put some

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:28.010
of the carrot top greens on
just for a little contrast.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:28.843
There's nothing else I can do.

00:10:28.843 --> 00:10:31.760
I'm gonna get the other
two courses and it's time

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.470
for Katie and Betsy to taste them.

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:34.303
Fingers crossed

00:10:34.303 --> 00:10:35.290
Betsy, Katie.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.123
- Yes.

00:10:36.123 --> 00:10:37.910
- I have made you a three course meal

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.810
using only five ingredients, as you know.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.410
- We've been watching it
and we've been impressed.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.727
- Exceeded expectations.

00:10:42.727 --> 00:10:44.670
It kind of looks like a full meal.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:46.073
- [Katie] Should we try
the appetizer first?

00:10:46.073 --> 00:10:48.990
- [Alexis] Chickpea
cornflake carrot fritters.

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:51.163
- [Katie] Mm. Nice crunch.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.502
- I, wow.

00:10:53.502 --> 00:10:54.740
- I really like that,
it's shockingly good.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:56.453
- I really, really like this

00:10:56.453 --> 00:10:58.500
- [Alexis] Main course.
I'm nervous about this one.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.450
- [Katie] I know you were skeptical

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.770
but I'm actually excited.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:02.155
Okay, cheers.

00:11:02.155 --> 00:11:02.988
- [Betsy] Cheers.

00:11:02.988 --> 00:11:03.821
- Oh my God.

00:11:03.821 --> 00:11:04.920
- That's a little, a wee bit salty.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.420
- [Betsy] I think the
shrimp are cooked perfectly.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:07.444
- And I don't mind the shrimp stock.

00:11:07.444 --> 00:11:11.280
- I find that the texture
of the noodles to be hard.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:12.113
- [Katie] Very excited for dessert.

00:11:12.113 --> 00:11:12.946
- [Katie And Betsy] Cheers.

00:11:12.946 --> 00:11:14.449
(Alexis laughs)

00:11:14.449 --> 00:11:16.740
(delighted moans)

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.780
- Oh, this is shockingly good.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.220
It's like foamy. It's crunchy.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.910
The cornflakes really worked out.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.010
- [Katie] Only five ingredients
in a three course meal.

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:25.843
- [Betsy] I'm impressed.

00:11:25.843 --> 00:11:26.680
- [Katie] And you made pasta.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.893
- One thing is for sure, I
cannot believe that you did this.

00:11:29.893 --> 00:11:33.610
- I feel really proud, but
if you want more recipes

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.590
kind of like this, I
have a cookbook coming

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:39.250
out April 19th and it's
all about, this very thing.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.642
Making the most of your ingredients

00:11:40.642 --> 00:11:43.841
in ways that are really
inspiring and delicious.

00:11:43.841 --> 00:11:45.530
- And we're so proud of you!
- I love that.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.790
- You can pre order in the link below

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.733
and if you wanna see me do
a challenge like this again

00:11:49.733 --> 00:11:50.566
let us know.

00:11:50.566 --> 00:11:52.483
- And now read your cookbook to us.

00:11:52.483 --> 00:11:55.184
(all laughing)

00:11:55.184 --> 00:11:58.017
(jazz tune plays)

